1- Observability is MELT (Metrics,Events,Logs,Traces) tool.

2- Observability provide dynamic visualization of system relationships : provides real time mapping of how services and infra components interact
within an IT env. 

3- Observability Agent runs as Daemonset in k8s monitored cluster ensuring complete cluster monitoring. 

4- Observability integrates natively with OpenTelemetry and ElasticSearch, and allows integartion with custom sources using configurable APIs.

5- Observability uses PVC on k8s to store the state of monitored components. 

6- Requirements:
   supported OS: SLES,Ubuntu and RHEL (use TLS version)
   linux kernel version 4.4+
   Helm 3.0+
   kubectl on nodes 
   containerd(prefered)/docker/cri-o
   curl
   jq 
   openSSL
   for architecture choose a profile from here: https://documentation.suse.com/cloudnative/suse-observability/latest/en/setup/install-stackstate/requirements.html#_resource_requirements
   for me now: I will used 3 nodes 8vCPU, 16GB each. (150-HA profile)
   use TLS for secure access to Observability
   DNS configured
   apply network policies if needed  to control inter-components communication
   for production SSD is recommended
   get license key

7- set a storage class frr Observability on RKE2. 

8- For prod env HA deployment are recommended as switching from non-HA to HA later isn't supported. 

9- store the baseConfig_values.yaml file and sizing_values.yaml file safely as they contain admin passwords and can be usable during upgrades.

10- you can install from helm. 

